<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{{ project_name }} — Jinax example</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/app.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="https://flaxon-website.vercel.app/assets/images/logo/flaxon.png" />
    <style>
      main { max-width: 760px; margin: 64px auto; padding: 24px; }
      p { line-height: 1.8; }
      nav { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 24px; margin-top: 32px; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <a href="https://flaxon-website.vercel.app/">
        <img src="https://flaxon-website.vercel.app/assets/images/logo/flaxon.png" alt="Flaxon" width="52" height="60" />
      </a>
      <h1>A complete page, rendered with Jinax.</h1>
      <p>Welcome to {{ project_name }}. Flaxon passed your project name to this HTML template, and Jinax rendered the response on the server.</p>
      <p>You can build your whole application this way: Python routes, HTML templates, forms, layouts, and your own JavaScript when you need it. Teloce is optional.</p>
      <p>This example does not load the Teloce runtime. The starter's main page demonstrates the other option: interactive HTML components and TypeScript compiled by Teloce.</p>
      <p>Edit <code>templates/welcome.html</code> and the <code>/server-page</code> route in <code>app.py</code> to make this page your own.</p>
      <nav>
        <a href="/">Back to the welcome page</a>
        <a href="/admin/login">Open your admin</a>
        <a href="https://flaxon-website.vercel.app/docs.html">Read the documentation</a>
      </nav>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
